// Light costs fuel. The headlamp burns fungus oil (180 s a measure): when a measure runs out it takes the
// next from the pack, then presses fungus into oil (2 fungus a measure), then goes dark. A torch needs a
// measure of oil to be lit. The log says when fungus is pressed, when the last measure goes in, and when it goes dark.
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#............................#
#...@........................#
##############################
end
mode survival
lamp 1 on
expect 1 lamp == 1
expect 1 oil > 179
expect 61 oil < 179.1
// run the lamp nearly dry: the next measure comes out of the pack
set 100 oil 0.5
expect 140 inv:FungusOil == 1
expect 140 oil > 178
// a torch soaks up a measure
placetorch 150 3 -2
expect 150 inv:Torch == 3
expect 150 inv:FungusOil == 0
expect 150 log:last_measure == 0     // (give is applied at the start: 2 fungus are still in the pack)
// no oil left: fungus is pressed instead
give Fungus 2
set 200 oil 0.5
expect 240 inv:Fungus == 0
expect 240 oil > 178
expect 240 log:pressed_2_fungus == 1
expect 240 log:last_measure == 1     // pressed the last of it
expect 240 log:a_workbench_presses_3_into_2 == 1   // and where to press more, better
// nothing left to burn: the lamp goes out, and a torch won't light
set 300 oil 0.5
expect 340 lamp == 0
expect 340 oil == 0
expect 340 log:out_of_oil == 1
expect 390 log:out_of_oil == 1     // once, not every tick
placetorch 350 6 -2
expect 350 inv:Torch == 3
// switched off, the lamp burns nothing
lamp 400 off
set 400 oil 10
expect 700 oil == 10
